STAGED LICENSE — NOT YET IN FORCE

This is the license intended to replace LICENSE once the pre-publication notice
is lifted. Until then LICENSE governs, and no license is granted.

To publish, in order:

  1. Replace LICENSE with everything below the line, and delete this file.
  2. Drop the pre-publication banner from the top of README.md.
  3. Fill in the issue-tracker URL in CONTRIBUTING.md, marked there with a
     `PUBLISH:` comment. Until that is done, a reader who finds an error has
     nowhere to send it.
  4. Re-run both gates and rebuild the bundle, so the shipped copy carries the
     real license rather than the notice.

Keep NOTICE as it is — it is attribution, not licensing, and it stands either
way.

Chosen for being as permissive as a license can reasonably be while still
carrying credit with every copy. A public-domain dedication (CC0) would be
marginally more open and was deliberately not used: it declares that the author
waives all rights they hold, which claims more about one author's authority over
a derived description of someone else's active product than is warranted here.
MIT makes the narrower, accurate claim — this writing is original and broadly
reusable — and its single obligation, preserving the notice, is what keeps the
pointer to NOTICE and SOURCE-AUTHORITY.md attached to any copy.

It covers the original expression in this repository: the prose, the structure,
and the tooling under tools/. It does not and cannot grant any right in the
manuals this material was learned from, which belong to their rights holders.
Facts about how a system behaves are not anyone's property; the words chosen to
describe them here are, and those are what is licensed.

